1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,890
If you lived in Salem in 1692, someone
else's nightmare could get you killed.

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:08,280
It began in winter. Two little girls began
to scream.

3
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:11,230
They twisted. They crawled beneath the
chairs.

4
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,950
They swore invisible hands were pinching
them in the dark.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,040
An enslaved woman named Tituba confessed.

6
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:23,080
A tall man in black showed her a book, and
she made her mark in it.

7
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:24,890
Soon, 50 more confessed.

8
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:28,880
Strangers searched their bodies for the
devil's mark,

9
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:32,950
and the witches of Salem burned. Or so the
story goes.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,670
But the records say otherwise. Not one
witch was burned in Salem.

11
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:43,190
Under English law, witchcraft was a
felony, and the punishment was the rope.

12
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,790
19 people were hanged.

13
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:49,950
One man, Giles Corey, was crushed beneath
stones for refusing to plead.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,470
The main proof: dreams and visions.

15
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:59,110
In 1697, a judge stood in church and
begged forgiveness.

16
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,530
The last name was cleared in 2022.

17
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,950
So, was there ever magic in Salem?

18
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,850
Or was fear the only spell that ever
worked? Real or myth?
